# Week 3 Cybersecurity | PDF Password Hash Extraction & Recovery
I'm pleased to share that I've completed another hands-on cybersecurity lab as part of my Network Walks Internship. In this practical exercise, I worked with three password protected PDF files and explored how password hashes can be extracted using different tools.

# Tools & Technologies Used:
John the Ripper
OnlineHashCrack

# Tasks Performed:
Extracted password hashes from password-protected PDF files using OnlineHashCrack
Used John the Ripper to start an attack
Reviewed and verified the password recovery results.

# Key Learning Outcomes:
Understanding password hashing and hash extraction.
Gaining practical experience with John the Ripper.
Understanding the importance of strong and unique passwords.
Strengthened the use of password security.

Grateful to NETWORKWALKS and Waqas Karim (CCIE) for providing practical learning opportunities and helping me strengthen my cybersecurity skills.
